Your most important priorities should be improving your armor
(AC should be negative as soon as possible) and then leveling
up.  There's no real rule with regards to the order of minetown
and Sokoban---with fighter classes, I tend to do the mines
first.  At level 4, and as a fighter, minetown shouldn't
represent too big a problem---if you get lucky and it is lit, no
problem at all.  And it will certainly allow you to improve your
armor: boots and a helmet are almost guaranteed, as is a cloak
(for MC and protecting metalic body armor from rust, even if it
doesn't improve your AC), and there's a good chance for mithral.
Plus a digging tool.

You'll want to get another pet eventually---there are things
you'll want dead (e.g. the minetown watch) for their death
drops, but that you don't want to kill yourself, because of
various penalties.  But there's no rush.

